{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792956044,"nonce":"MUb/jerzZy7p4+MNhE+69jhQg+s=","title":"Virtualize Settings lists and keep browser navigation responsive","message":"Rapid Settings navigation stalls the browser UI. The selected section is already the only one mounted, but Key bindings constructed every command row and Libraries every library row. The navigation itself was also rebuilt on every selection. Installed library discovery could synchronously start and read a process during rendering; extension configuration reread workspace/user settings for each field.\n\nBefore/after in headless Chrome, 1280x800, three Ash agents, same local build/toolchain and page agent:\n- Key bindings mounted 92 rows before and 17 after. Three readiness samples: 691/664/679 ms before; 179/183/166 ms after.\n- The quick-switch burst reached its final page in 776 ms before and 238 ms after.\n- The shared event ring stayed small (peak 792 bytes) with no failed or dropped records. Input p95/max went from about 658 ms to 162 ms. The queue waited for UI work; capacity/lost events were not the bottleneck in this reproduction.\n- Remote workspace run also passed: extension service round trip, asynchronous real haxelib query, bounded rows, final navigation target and no dropped input. Final burst about 266 ms, queue max 720 bytes and input max about 176 ms.\n\nImplementation: fixed-height viewport rows with spacer geometry and overscan for command/library lists, stable Settings navigation identities, one shared ash.Future catalog query with refresh generation protection, apply catalog results during UI flushes, and one settings read per scope for an extension form. Inactive sections still dispose their elements rather than accumulating hidden pages.\n\nBrowser reach: RayDE Explorer/Command Center and the new Settings windowing are shared Haxe code with no wasm exclusion. Ashui calls the same native display-list/clip-culling ABI on wasm; draw culling does not prevent creation/style/layout of all rows. The new browser probe confirms bounded mounted rows on the actual wasm path.\n\nChecks: SettingsChecks mounts 1000 commands and 200 libraries, reaches final rows, filters offscreen commands, switches repeatedly with bounded element counts, preserves nav node ids, navigates while a catalog query is pending, shares concurrent queries, rejects stale refresh results, and verifies batched form reads. xwindow's three page-agent tests pass, including pressure coalescing and press/release ordering. Probe artifacts: bin/web/settings-measured-before, settings-measured-after, settings-remote.","files":null}]}